        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Two halves of a man's waistcoat, 1770s, British, ivory silk satin embroidered with coloured silks, altered 1870-1910"@en , "Two halves of a man’s waistcoat made of ivory silk satin embroidered with coloured silks in a floral pattern.  The waistcoat was altered for fancy dress in the 19th century. The skirts were cut off, the back and buttons replaced."@en ;
